Blockquote example: Reproducible work makes it easier for someone else (or future me) to rerun the same workflow and confirm results.

I learned what it means to have reproducible data versus replicable data. In data science reproducible is an output that yields the same results while the source code and data remain unchanged. Replicable is when output remains the same while the data is changing. Tools like R Markdown or Jupyter Notebooks combine code with natural language (prose), explaining the "why" behind the analysis rather than just the "how"

::: callout-note
With the use of scripts in R or python you can make data visualization much faster. You can also go use Github for collaboration and archival, also allowing for version control.
:::

